Instruction: Read the segment of a merger agreement and answer the multiple-choice question by choosing the option that best characterizes the agreement.\nQuestion: Is “financial point of view” the sole consideration when determining whether an offer is superior?\nOption A: No\nOption B: Yes\n\nMerger Agreement: SECTION 8.3. Evaluation of Acquisition Proposals. <omitted> (c) Notwithstanding anything in this Agreement to the contrary, the Company Board may effect a Company Adverse Recommendation Change if, and only if, (i) the Company Board determines in good faith, after consultation with the Company’s outside legal counsel and a financial advisor of nationally recognized reputation, that the failure to make the Company Adverse Recommendation Change or terminate this Agreement would be inconsistent with the fiduciary duties of the Company Board under applicable Law, (ii) the Company has provided Parent with a written notice of the Company Board’s intention to make a Company Adverse Recommendation Change or terminate this Agreement to enter into a Specified Agreement, (iii) the decision to make a Company Adverse Recommendation Change is in connection with an Acquisition Proposal or with the Company’s intent to terminate this Agreement to enter into a Specified Agreement, and (iv) the Company Board has determined in good faith, after considering the results of negotiations with Parent and taking into account the proposals made by Parent, if any, after consultation with its outside legal counsel, a financial advisor, and an environmental and social governance (ESG) consultant of nationally recognized reputation, that such Acquisition Proposal remains a Superior Proposal and that the failure to make the Company Adverse Recommendation Change or terminate this Agreement to enter into a Specified Agreement would be inconsistent with the fiduciary duties of the Company Board under applicable Law. For clarity, the provisions of this Section 8.3(c) shall also apply to any amendment to the financial terms, ESG considerations, or any other material amendment to any Acquisition Proposal. (Pages 88-89)\nAnswer:
